 ### Astrology engine
 
-`@zodiacs/engine` candidate version 0.1.1-rc.1 is the pure-TypeScript calculation sibling. It is browser-first, Node-compatible, ESM-only, synchronous, side-effect-free, and tree-shakeable. The core entry makes no network request. It computes apparent geocentric tropical positions, natal charts, transits, synastry, lunar phase, and Saturn-return seasons. Whole-sign and Placidus houses are supported; Placidus falls back to whole sign above 66° absolute latitude and returns the `polar-fallback` flag.
+`@zodiacs/engine` candidate version 0.1.1-rc.5 is the pure-TypeScript calculation sibling. It is browser-first, Node-compatible, ESM-only, synchronous, side-effect-free, and tree-shakeable. The core entry makes no network request. It computes apparent geocentric tropical positions, natal charts, transits, synastry, lunar phase, and Saturn-return seasons. Whole-sign and Placidus houses are supported; Placidus falls back to whole sign above 66° absolute latitude and returns the `polar-fallback` flag.
 
-Typed API reference: https://zodiacs.org/sdk/engine/
+Current candidate API guide: https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/blob/97f5e8d01828f4b85ffa845825dee9acff4695e4/packages/engine/README.md
+
+Optional `@zodiacs/engine/receipt` validates a Zodiacs-owned draft natal envelope from a fresh full public Chart. It preserves requested versus actual houses, unknown-time reference instants and supplied provenance; it does not authenticate claims or recalculate positions. The site saved-chart/account format is unchanged, and the standalone starter retains its separately pinned engine rc.3. Draft specification: https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/blob/97f5e8d01828f4b85ffa845825dee9acff4695e4/docs/platform/receipt-draft-v1.md
+
+Archived rc.1 typed API reference (earlier candidate): https://zodiacs.org/sdk/engine/
 
 Licensing chain: the engine uses MIT-licensed Astronomy Engine and explicitly excludes Swiss Ephemeris code. `@zodiacs/engine/geo` contains adapters, not a bundled place database. GeoNames-derived place data is CC BY 4.0; downstream users must retain the package `NOTICE`. Historical timezone resolution depends on the host's IANA/ICU data.
 
-Release status: this site revision consumes an exact vendored `@zodiacs/engine@0.1.1-rc.1` npm pack artifact and verifies its checksum. It is an unpublished review candidate, not a verified npm release. Agents must verify publication, or use the exact repository artifact documented in `vendor/README.md`, until an authorized maintainer publishes it.
+Release status: this site revision consumes an exact vendored `@zodiacs/engine@0.1.1-rc.5` npm pack artifact and verifies its checksum. It is an unpublished review candidate, not a verified npm release. Agents must verify publication, or use the exact repository artifact documented in `vendor/README.md`, until an authorized maintainer publishes it.
 
